# GTO - Git-based Tracking of Data Changes

GTO is a simple, powerful system for tracking data changes in your Python projects. Just import it and everything else happens automatically!

## Quick Start

```bash
# Install
pip install gto

# Run demo
python run_gto.py
```

That's it! The demo will show you GTO in action.

## Project Structure

```
gto/
├── src/gto/        # Main package code
│   ├── core/       # Core functionality
│   ├── data/       # Data handling
│   └── reporting/  # Change reporting
├── tests/          # Test suite
├── docs/           # Documentation
├── examples/       # Example data and scripts
└── run_gto.py      # Quick demo script
```

## Features

- **Automatic Change Detection**: GTO automatically detects when your data files change
- **Human-Readable Reports**: Get clear, narrative reports of what changed in your data
- **Historical Tracking**: Maintain a complete history of all data modifications
- **Documentation**: Automatic generation of comprehensive documentation
- **Repository Sync**: Keep multiple repositories in sync with your data

## Detailed Usage

```python
import gto  # This automatically sets up monitoring

# Your regular pandas code works as usual
import pandas as pd
df = pd.read_csv('data.csv')  # Changes are automatically tracked
```

## Documentation

Documentation is automatically generated in the `docs/build/html` directory. You can view it by opening `docs/build/html/index.html` in your browser.

## Development

To set up for development:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/yourusername/gto.git
cd gto
pip install -e .
```

Run tests:
```bash
python -m pytest tests/
```

